{"c":[{"id":"c6f40c96b6283efc","sum":"B28b/D2-04: EXCLUSION_WORDS end name trust; SECTION trusts only fields of its meaning. A control's value never rides FillField.value. A box gets a tick only for a question to the user (boxKind). accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6936d2244b2292af","sum":"B28b: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word (scope-words.ts) gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value; Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4fad04d8f129b479","sum":"D2-04: a box gets a tick only when its label is a question to the user (fill/controls.ts boxKind); never widen it by adding consent words. accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8f8d8cc08d8e1b1","sum":"D2-04/B29: radio peers found tree-wide by name+form owner; ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput (undo refuses); number fields compare numerically for undo only; RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' (tests say 'not from X').","tree":{"c":[{"id":"50990865af94b806","sum":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner (the form attribute). B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the intended value; a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it, as for pre-B29 rows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields compare as numbers for undo identity only (executor.ts canonicalDecimal, not Number()); sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X' (no source question), so excluded-window tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
